{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A setup command that modifies tracked files can make the reviewer assess different contents from the labelled revision, leading to missed or incorrect findings."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Comparing setup and control arms for the same reviewer can make generated routing policy depend on trial order rather than reliable evidence."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Replaying findings across different setup settings silently mislabels the measured environment and can produce a misleading evaluation result."}]}